-- title:
--   Reducedness of the geometric special fibre of a two-chart model
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, with perfect residue field, let $\varpi \in R$ satisfy $\mathfrak{m}_R = (\varpi)$, let $K_0$ be a fraction field of $R$, and let $F$ be a field which is an $R$- and a $K_0$-algebra compatibly. Let $j \in F$ be nonzero and transcendental over $R$, and assume $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K_0(j)$. Write $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ for `chartAlgFin R F j`, the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over $R[j]$, and $A_{\mathrm{inf}}$ for `chartAlgInf R F j`, the elements of $F$ integral over $R[j^{-1}]$. Assume that for every prime $P$ of $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ minimal over the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$, the image of that ideal in the localisation $(A_{\mathrm{fin}})_P$ is the maximal ideal, and likewise for every such minimal prime of $A_{\mathrm{inf}}$. Finally let $\kappa$ be a field which is an $R$-algebra with $\varpi \mapsto 0$. Then the scheme-theoretic pullback of `toBase R F j`, the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} R$ of the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the two chart inclusions into the middle chart, along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $R \to \kappa$ is a reduced scheme.
--
--   This is the reducedness criterion for the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of a curve over a discrete valuation ring: if the uniformiser has multiplicity one along every component of both affine charts, then every fibre over a field killing $\varpi$ — in particular the geometric special fibre — is reduced. It is applied to the integral models of modular curves, being cited in the reducedness statements for $X_1(p)$-type models and for the fibres of Hecke degeneracy maps.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_isReduced_pullback_toBase_of_forall_map_span_eq_maximalIdeal.lean

